# EXPECT-VIOLATION: mirash:RegisterInterpretationShape
#
# R5 — a register actually USED as an engineering value (it `decodes` a signal) but carrying no
# datatype, no ScalingRule and no unit. GS10 DC-bus raw 6000 is 600.0 V at scaling 0.01;
# unscaled it reads as a ten-fold overvoltage that does not exist. Signed vs unsigned differs
# by 65536.
#
# A register catalogued WITHOUT a decode is honest incompleteness and is deliberately not
# targeted — see the valid counterpart.

@prefix mira: <https://ontology.factorylm.com/mira#> .
@prefix xsd:  <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix ex:   <https://example.org/fx#> .

ex:dc_bus  a mira:MeasurementSignal .
ex:reg_bad a mira:Register ; mira:decodes ex:dc_bus ; mira:register_addr 2103 .
